:: 1.1 Start [between] {"position":"100,250","size":"100,100"}
<div class="title">DE MORTUIS</div>
<span class="dissolve">nil nisi bonum</span>

[[Begin->1.2 The voice]]


:: 1.10 What you gave {"position":"100,1500","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.10 · What you gave</span>

(if: $gave)[You say it like it's nothing. Scholarship. Money. Might be leaving.

She leans in so close you can smell her shampoo. "No way," she says, kind of excited. "Poor thing."

She's nicer to you for the rest of the night than she's ever been. (if: $slip >= 3)[You tell yourself it's fine. It's just one person. person.](else:)[You tell yourself it's fine. It's just one person.]](else:)["Honestly, there's nothing," you say.

She looks at you a second too long, then leans back. "Boring," she says, but not in a mean way. The rest of the night is flat. She checks her phone twice.

You walk home alone. You feel proud of yourself and lonely at the same time.]

[[Continue->1.11 Back in the between]]


:: 1.11 Back in the between [between] {"position":"100,1650","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.11 · Back in the between</span>

The memory closes behind you.

(if: $spent)[<span class="voice">You're good at this. Everyone always says you're a good listener.</span>](else:)[<span class="voice">Well. That was something.</span>]

<span class="voice">Take your time. Kind of.</span>

(if: $strength <= 2)[Your hands look thinner than they did. You can almost see the dark through them.]

(if: $slip >= 2)[When you look back at the common room window, the TV has sound now. It was muted before.]

[[Enter week 2: the library->2.1 Naomi notices]]


:: 1.2 The voice [between] {"position":"100,400","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.2 · The voice</span>

There's no floor. No walls. You're not really standing on anything, you're just kind of there. It's quiet, like a room right after someone walks out.

Then a voice. Close. Like someone leaning in to tell you a secret.

<span class="voice">Hey, there you are. Don't freak out, it doesn't help.</span>

<span class="voice">So. You're dead. Sorry. That's the big news.</span>

<span class="voice">Here's the good part though. You get to go back. Not to live it again, just to look. Your last month is still in here, all of it. Some of it you remember fine. Some of it you've been lying to yourself about. If you want, you can look at those parts through someone else's eyes.</span>

<span class="voice">And if you look close enough, you might get to change one thing. Just one. After that it's locked.</span>

<span class="voice">Oh, and be careful whose eyes you borrow. What they felt comes back with you. And you don't have forever in here.</span>

You can hear it smiling.

<span class="voice">I'll be right here. Tell me something interesting when you get back.</span>

(link-reveal-goto: "\"Where am I?\"", "1.3 The between")[(set: $asked to "where")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"How did I die?\"", "1.3 The between")[(set: $asked to "how")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Say nothing", "1.3 The between")[(set: $asked to "nothing")]


:: 1.3 The between [between] {"position":"100,550","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.3 · The between</span>

(if: $asked is "where")[<span class="voice">In between. That's not me being cute, that's what it's called.</span>](else-if: $asked is "how")[<span class="voice">Does it matter? It's in here somewhere. Maybe you'll find it.</span>](else:)[<span class="voice">Strong silent type. Okay. I can work with that.</span>]

All around you there are memories floating in the dark, like windows with the lights on. Some are sharp. Some are smudged, like someone breathed on the glass.

You know all of them. The common room. The café. The library. A party. The back steps. A door with a sticker half peeled off.

You're just not sure how you feel about any of them.

[[Enter week 1: the common room->1.4 Iris tells you]]


:: 1.4 Iris tells you {"position":"100,700","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.4 · Iris tells you · Common room, 11 pm</span>

The common room smells like microwave popcorn and somebody's laundry. The TV's on but muted. Everyone else went to bed an hour ago.

Iris is sitting sideways on the armchair with her knees pulled up. Her blue hair is in a messy bun. She's been weirdly quiet all night.

"Can I tell you something?" she says. "Just you. Not the others."

"Yeah, of course." You always say of course.

"I lost my scholarship. Got the email this morning. My parents don't know yet." She laughs, but it doesn't sound right. "If I can't figure out the money by December, I have to leave. You're literally the only person I've told."

The memory is clear up to here. After that it goes blurry, like you stopped paying attention.

[[Just listen->1.7 Pick your date]]
(if: $strength > 0)[ [[See through Iris (it will cost you)->1.5 Iris's side]] ]


:: 1.5 Iris's side {"position":"300,800","size":"100,100"}
(set: $strength to it - 1, $slip to it + 1, $sawIris to true)<span class="act">ACT 1.5 · Iris's side</span>

Everything looks different from her chair. The room feels smaller. The TV is way too bright.

She practiced this in the shower three times. She picked you because you never make things weird. Because you keep everything to yourself. Telling you feels like locking something in a drawer.

When you say "of course," her shoulders drop a little. She thinks: //Okay. At least one person knows. At least it's you.//

(if: $strength > 0)[ [[Look deeper (it will cost you)->1.6 Later that night]] ]
[[Leave her->1.7 Pick your date]]


:: 1.6 Later that night {"position":"300,950","size":"100,100"}
(set: $strength to it - 1, $slip to it + 1, $sawDeeper to true)<span class="act">ACT 1.6 · Later that night</span>

You go deeper. It's harder in here. You've already gone to bed, but she's still on the armchair going over the conversation again.

There's a part you cut out of your own memory. In her head it's loud: "I haven't really been sleeping. I keep thinking everyone would be fine if I just left. Like, it'd be easier."

Then you hear yourself answer. "Don't be dramatic." And then you changed the subject to the party on Friday. She laughed along. Inside she thought: //Okay. Noted.//

You didn't forget this. You just chose not to remember it. And now you can't unhear it.

[[Leave the memory->1.7 Pick your date]]


:: 1.7 Pick your date {"position":"100,1050","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.7 · Pick your date · Café, 5 pm</span>

The café by the quad is loud and warm and too small. Your group has a corner table that isn't technically yours, but everyone acts like it is.

There are three people you've been thinking about asking out.

''Maeve.'' White hair, laughs at literally everything you say. Always wants to know what's going on with everyone.

''Naomi.'' Sharp and funny. The only one who ever asks how //you're// doing.

''Iris.'' Who told you her biggest secret two nights ago.

(link-reveal-goto: "Ask Maeve", "1.8 Your date")[(set: $date to "Maeve")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Ask Naomi", "1.8 Your date")[(set: $date to "Naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Ask Iris", "1.8 Your date")[(set: $date to "Iris")]


:: 1.8 Your date {"position":"100,1200","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 1.8 · Your date · Café</span>

(if: $date is "Maeve")[She says yes before you even finish asking. She stirs her coffee but never drinks it.

"So," she says, chin on her hand. "Tell me something interesting. What's up with everyone? Iris has been so quiet lately."

Her eyes are super pale. She's completely focused on you, and honestly it feels great.](else-if: $date is "Naomi")[She raises an eyebrow, then says yes. She actually eats her muffin.

"You look tired," she says. "You always look like you're carrying everyone's stuff." She means it in a nice way.

Then Maeve walks past the table and goes, "Ooh, are we sharing secrets? Tell her about Iris." She's gone before you can ask how she even knows there's something to tell.](else:)[She blinks. Then she actually smiles for the first time all week. "Okay," she says. "Yeah. Okay."

You spend an hour talking about nothing. It's easy. Near the end, Maeve slides into the booth next to you without asking. "Aww, cute. So are you two telling each other everything now?"

Iris goes quiet.]

[[Continue->1.9 Tell me something]]


:: 1.9 Tell me something {"position":"100,1350","size":"100,100"}
(unless: $rewriteUsed)[(set: $s19 to (a: $slip, $distance))]<span class="act">ACT 1.9 · Tell me something · Café, 6 pm</span>

(if: $date is not "Maeve")[Later, Maeve catches you alone at the counter.

]"Come on," she says. "You know everything about everyone. That's why people like you. Just give me one thing."

Iris's secret is right there. It'd be so easy. It'd make this moment even better.

(link-reveal-goto: "Give up Iris's secret", "1.10 What you gave")[(set: $gave to true, $spent to true, $slip to it + 2)]
(link-reveal-goto: "Stay quiet", "1.10 What you gave")[(set: $gave to false, $spent to false, $distance to it + 1)]


:: 2.1 Naomi notices {"position":"600,100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $act to 2)<span class="act">ACT 2.1 · Naomi notices · Library, 3 pm</span>

The quiet floor. The radiators keep ticking. Naomi has taken over a table by the window, and it's covered in highlighters.

She doesn't look up when you sit down. "Can I say something without you getting weird about it?"

(if: $spent)["People are talking about Iris," she says. "Not nice stuff. And the stuff they know... I feel like only you would know it." Then she looks up. "I'm not accusing you. I'm just asking you to be careful."](else:)["People keep asking me what's wrong with Iris," she says. "You're closest to her. Whatever she told you, just keep it to yourself, okay?"]

(link-reveal-goto: "Listen to her", "2.3 It spreads")[(set: $lib to "listen", $slip to (max: 0, it - 1))]
(link-reveal-goto: "Change the subject", "2.3 It spreads")[(set: $lib to "change", $naomiGaveUp to true, $distance to it + 1)]
(if: $strength > 0)[ [[See through Naomi (it will cost you)->2.2 Naomi's side]] ]


:: 2.2 Naomi's side {"position":"800,250","size":"100,100"}
(set: $strength to it - 1, $slip to it + 1, $sawNaomi to true, $lib to "see")<span class="act">ACT 2.2 · Naomi's side</span>

Her heart is going really fast. She practiced this.

She's watched the rumor go around the group for a week, and she's already figured it out. There's only one person Iris would have told. And Naomi likes that person. That's why this is so hard.

She thinks: //If the answer's a lie, I'll know. And then I have to figure out what we even are.//

[[Leave her->2.3 It spreads]]


:: 2.3 It spreads {"position":"600,400","size":"100,100"}
(unless: $rewriteUsed)[(set: $s23 to (a: $slip, $distance))]<span class="act">ACT 2.3 · It spreads · Party house, 11 pm</span>

(if: $lib is "listen")["I'll be careful," you told her. "I promise." She nodded and went back to her notes. You meant it. Pretty sure you meant it.](else-if: $lib is "change")[You asked about the reading for Thursday. Naomi answered, and she never brought up Iris again.](else:)[The conversation just ended. Neither of you said it.]

Bass coming through the floor. A kitchen full of people you sort of know. Someone put fairy lights around the fridge.

Iris is sitting on the stairs holding a cup she isn't drinking. From across the room you hear her name. And a version of her secret that isn't even hers anymore.

(if: $spent)["She got caught cheating. That's why they took her scholarship. She's getting kicked out."

None of that is true. All of it started with something that was.](else:)["Iris is leaving. Something about money."

Nobody knows where it came from. Maeve won't say where she heard it.]

Maeve is in the middle of the group, laughing, her white hair catching the light. She sees you and waves you over.

(link-reveal-goto: "Defend Iris", "2.5 Meanwhile")[(set: $party to "defend", $slip to (max: 0, it - 1))]
(link-reveal-goto: "Laugh along", "2.5 Meanwhile")[(set: $party to "laugh", $slip to it + 2)]
(if: $strength > 0)[ [[See through Maeve (it will cost you)->2.4 Maeve's mind]] ]


:: 2.4 Maeve's mind {"position":"800,550","size":"100,100"}
(set: $strength to it - 1, $slip to it + 2, $party to "maeve")<span class="act">ACT 2.4 · Maeve's mind</span>

You reach for her the same way you would with anyone else.

Nothing.

Not dark. Not quiet. Just you, standing in the kitchen, seen from very close. Your own face, looking back at you.

You pull out fast. The party is too loud now.

[[Continue->2.5 Meanwhile]]


:: 2.5 Meanwhile {"position":"600,700","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 2.5 · Meanwhile</span>

(if: $party is "defend")["That's not what happened," you say. "Leave her alone."

Everyone goes quiet. Someone says "okay, sorry" the way people do when they're not sorry. Maeve tilts her head at you like you just did a trick.](else-if: $party is "laugh")[You don't actually say anything that's a lie. You just laugh at the right time. When someone asks "wait, is it true?" you shrug in a way that basically means yes.

(if: $slip >= 4)[(if: $sawDeeper)[<span class="echo2">don't be dramatic</span>](else:)[<span class="echo2">you're the only one I told</span>]

]Everyone turns to look at the stairs. Iris is already gone.](else:)[You don't say anything. Everyone just keeps talking without you.]

Then the memory closes.

While you were in there, the story kept going without you.

You get a look at the group chat. The real one, from after. Messages flying. Iris's name over and over. Someone posts a screenshot. Someone says //"guys stop"//. Nobody stops.
(if: $slip >= 4)[<span class="echo2">you're the only one I told</span>]

<span class="voice">It doesn't wait for you. Stories never do.</span>

[[Enter week 3: the back steps->3.1 Who told?]]


:: 3.1 Who told? {"position":"1250,100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $act to 3)(unless: $rewriteUsed)[(set: $s31 to (a: $slip, $distance))]<span class="act">ACT 3.1 · Who told? · Back steps, 1 am</span>

Cold concrete. A motion light that only works if you wave at it. A coffee can full of cigarette butts that nobody admits are theirs.

Iris is on the bottom step. She texted you //can you come outside// and nothing else. Her eyes are red, but her voice is steady, which is somehow worse.

(if: $party is "defend")["People are saying stuff about me," she says quietly. "About the scholarship. I don't know what to do."

She looks up at you.

"You're the only one I told. Can you help me figure out who else knows?"](else:)["Someone told people," she says. "About the scholarship. They're saying I cheated. My RA asked if I was okay. People I don't even know are staring at me in the dining hall."

She looks up at you.

"You're the only one I told. So I need you to tell me who you told."](if: $date is "Iris")[

"I thought we were... I don't even know what I thought."]

(if: $slip >= 4)[(if: $sawDeeper)[<span class="echo2">don't be dramatic</span>](else:)[<span class="echo2">you're the only one I told</span>]]

(if: $spent)[ [[Tell her what really happened->3.2 What really happened]] ](else:)[ [[Tell her you didn't tell anyone, but you didn't stop it either->3.2 What really happened]] ]
[[Comfort her, stay quiet->3.3 The lie]]
[[Blame Maeve->3.4 New victim]]
[[Walk away->3.5 Distance]]


:: 3.2 What really happened {"position":"1100,250","size":"100,100"}
(set: $slip to (max: 0, it - 2))<span class="act">ACT 3.2 · What really happened</span>

(if: $spent)["It was me," you say. "I told Maeve. I didn't think it would... I'm sorry."](else:)["I didn't tell anyone," you say. "But I heard it going around, and I didn't stop it. I'm sorry."]

Iris doesn't yell. She just nods, like she already knew. She stands up.

"Thank you for telling me," she says. "I need to not be around you for a bit."

She goes inside. The motion light clicks off.

It's the worst you've ever felt. It's also the first honest thing you've done all month.

[[Continue->3.6 Sawyer leaves]]


:: 3.3 The lie {"position":"1400,250","size":"100,100"}
(set: $slip to it + 2)<span class="act">ACT 3.3 · The lie</span>

"I didn't tell anyone," you say. "I swear. People just talk. Come here."

She leans into you. She believes you. That's what gets you.

(if: $slip >= 4)[On the way back to your room, the hallway feels longer than it should. The lights hum. The lights hum. You keep hearing her say //you're the only one I told you're the only one I told(if: $slip >= 6)[ you're the only one I <span class="echo3">TOLD</span>]//](else:)[You walk back to your room. The hallway is quiet.]

[[Continue->3.6 Sawyer leaves]]


:: 3.4 New victim {"position":"1100,400","size":"100,100"}
(set: $slip to it + 2)<span class="act">ACT 3.4 · New victim</span>

"Maeve," you say. "She kept asking about you. I think she overheard us."

Iris's jaw goes tight. "Of course it was her."

The next day the whole group turns on Maeve. Nobody sits with her. And Maeve doesn't care at all. She smiles at you from across the café like you just gave her a present.

Nothing sticks to her. Nothing ever has.

[[Continue->3.6 Sawyer leaves]]


:: 3.5 Distance {"position":"1400,400","size":"100,100"}
(set: $distance to it + 2)<span class="act">ACT 3.5 · Distance</span>

You don't say anything. You just stand there too long. Then you say "I gotta go," and you go.

She doesn't follow you.

You stop answering the group chat that night.

[[Continue->3.6 Sawyer leaves]]


:: 3.6 Sawyer leaves {"position":"1250,550","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 3.6 · Sawyer leaves · Café, 10 am</span>

Same corner table as always. Except Sawyer's chair is pushed in, and his hoodie isn't on the back of it.

He walks in, sees you, and doesn't sit down. He's got his bag on.

"I'm gonna do my own thing for a while," he says. "This isn't really a friend group anymore. It's just people watching each other."

He's out the door before anyone says anything.

(if: $date is "Naomi")[Naomi is the only one who looks at you instead of the door. (if: $naomiGaveUp)[She looks away first.](else:)[She doesn't look away.]
]
(link-reveal-goto: "Go after him", "3.7 The door")[(set: $sawyer to "follow", $distance to (max: 0, it - 1))]
(link-reveal-goto: "Let him go", "3.7 The door")[(set: $sawyer to "let", $distance to it + 1)]
(if: $strength > 0)[ [[See through Sawyer (it will cost you)->3.8 Sawyer's side]] ]


:: 3.7 The door {"position":"1250,700","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 3.7 · The door · Café doorway</span>

(if: $sawyer is "follow")[You catch him at the door.

(if: $spent)["I saw you," he says, not looking at you. "At the café, first week. With Maeve. I saw your face when you told her. You looked happy."](else:)["I saw you at the party," he says, not looking at you. "You didn't say anything. Neither did I."]

He's holding the door open. He doesn't leave, and he doesn't come back in either.

"I didn't say anything either. So I guess we're the same."](else:)[Nobody says his name after that. His chair stays pushed in for a week, then someone takes it to another table.

It's easier than you thought it would be. That's the scary part.]

[[Continue->4.1 The between, later]]


:: 3.8 Sawyer's side {"position":"1450,700","size":"100,100"}
(set: $strength to it - 1, $slip to it + 1, $sawSawyer to true)<span class="act">ACT 3.8 · Sawyer's side</span>

He's been keeping track. Who talks to who. Who goes quiet when someone walks in. Everything goes through one person. You.

He likes you. He always has. That's why he's leaving instead of saying it.

He thinks: //If I stay, I'm part of it.//

[[Leave him->4.1 The between, later]]


:: 4.1 The between, later [between] {"position":"1800,100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $act to 4)<span class="act">ACT 4.1 · The between, later</span>

(if: $slip >= 6)[(if: $sawIris)[<span class="echo1">at least it's you</span> ](if: $sawDeeper)[<span class="echo2">don't be dramatic</span> ](if: $sawNaomi)[<span class="echo2">I'll know</span> ](if: $sawSawyer)[<span class="echo3">IF I STAY</span>]

](if: $strength <= 0)[You reach for another memory and your hand just doesn't get there. The windows go dark one by one. Whatever you saw, whatever you missed, that's how it stays.

Except one. Your room. Your phone, lit up on the nightstand. That one doesn't need anything from you except an answer.

<span class="voice">That's okay. Most people don't make it this far.</span>

[[Keep going->4.3 The last text]]
[[Let go->4.4 After]]](else:)[There are fewer windows now. Some went dark on their own while you weren't looking.

You hold up your hand. You can see the memories through it.

<span class="voice">Aw, you're getting see-through. Honestly, I could always see right through you.</span>

(unless: $rewriteUsed)[<span class="voice">You can still change something if you want. One thing. It's going to take a lot out of you. No pressure.</span>

 [[Rewrite a scene->4.2 Rewrite]]
]
[[Keep going->4.3 The last text]]
[[Let go->4.4 After]]]


:: 4.2 Rewrite [between] {"position":"2000,250","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 4.2 · Rewrite</span>

You pick a moment and step back into your own body in it. It fits weird, like a jacket that used to be yours.

You can go back into one of these. Only one. Everything after it plays out again.

(link-reveal-goto: "Tell me something: the café", "1.9 Tell me something")[(set: $rewriteUsed to true, $strength to it - 1, $act to 1, $slip to $s19's 1st, $distance to $s19's 2nd)]
(link-reveal-goto: "It spreads: the party", "2.3 It spreads")[(set: $rewriteUsed to true, $strength to it - 1, $act to 2, $slip to $s23's 1st, $distance to $s23's 2nd)]
(link-reveal-goto: "Who told?: the back steps", "3.1 Who told?")[(set: $rewriteUsed to true, $strength to it - 1, $slip to $s31's 1st, $distance to $s31's 2nd)]

[[Change your mind->4.3 The last text]]


:: 4.3 The last text {"position":"1800,400","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 4.3 · The last text · Your room, 2:07 am</span>

Your room is dark except for your phone. You were almost asleep.

It buzzes once.

<span class="phone">''Iris:'' are you up</span>

The three dots show up. Go away. Show up again.

<span class="phone">''Iris:'' nvm. sorry for being a lot this month</span>

You remember this. You remember exactly what you did the first time.

(link-reveal-goto: "Answer: \"I'm here. Want me to come over?\"", "4.4 After")[(set: $answered to true, $distance to (max: 0, it - 1))]
(link-reveal-goto: "Leave it on read", "4.4 After")[(set: $answered to false, $distance to it + 1)]


:: 4.4 After {"position":"1800,550","size":"100,100"}
(set: $onTrack to ($slip <= 2 and $distance <= 2 and $answered))<span class="act">ACT 4.4 · After · Common room, a few days later</span>

(if: $answered and not $onTrack)[She texted back. //its fine go to sleep.// And the night went the same way.

](if: $onTrack)[The common room smells like microwave popcorn. The TV is on mute. Iris is sitting sideways on the armchair with her knees up, telling Naomi about a payment plan with financial aid.

She sees you and doesn't smile. Not yet. But she moves her feet so you can sit down.](else:)[The common room is full and nobody's talking. Naomi is crying without making any noise. Sawyer came back. Someone left flowers in the hallway, outside a door with a sticker half peeled off.

Nobody says how. Nobody has to.

Everyone in the room is going back over the same month, looking for the one moment that did it. There isn't one. There were a hundred, and they weren't all yours.

The memory stops there. You can't find anything after it.]

[[Continue->4.5 The reveal]]


:: 4.5 The reveal [between] {"position":"1800,700","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">ACT 4.5 · The reveal</span>

The last window closes. It's just you and the dark.

<span class="voice">So. Tell me something interesting.</span>

And then, for the first time, she steps out where you can see her. White hair. Pale eyes. The coffee she never drank.

Maeve.

<span class="voice-clear">"You figured it out kind of late," she says. "People usually do."</span> She sits down on nothing. <span class="voice-clear">"I never lied to you, by the way. Okay, maybe the dead part. That was never decided. That was always up to you."</span> She shrugs. <span class="voice-clear">"Mostly I just asked. You're the one who kept answering."</span>

She tilts her head at you, the same way she did at the party. <span class="voice-clear">"So. How'd you do?"</span>

(if: $date is "Maeve")[<span class="voice-clear">"You were a really good date, by the way. I mean it."</span>](else:)[<span class="voice-clear">"I was at every table. You just never looked at me long enough."</span>]

<span class="voice-clear">"Okay,"</span> she says. <span class="voice-clear">"Let's see where you ended up."</span>

(if: $onTrack)[ [[Continue->4.6 Holds]] ](else-if: $slip >= 5)[ [[Continue->4.8 Comes apart]] ](else:)[ [[Continue->4.7 Pulls away]] ]


:: 4.6 Holds {"position":"1600,850","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">Ending · Holds · Common room, March</span>

You wake up on the couch with the TV on. Your phone says it's March.

You're here. So is Iris. She still doesn't fully trust you, and maybe she never will. But when Naomi asks who wants food, Iris says your name with everyone else's.

Maeve isn't in any of the group photos anymore. Nobody remembers her being in them.

<span class="voice">Huh,</span> the voice says, very quiet and very far away. Then nothing.

[[The end->Credits]]


:: 4.7 Pulls away {"position":"1800,850","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">Ending · Pulls away · Your room, a few weeks later</span>

You're transferring. Your room is just boxes and a bare mattress. Your parents are coming Saturday.

You're alive. You don't know if Iris is. You never asked. You left the group chat, and nobody at the new school is going to know anything about you. You're keeping it that way.

The page is almost empty.

<span class="voice">Safe,</span> the voice says, sounding a little bored. <span class="voice">Lonely, but safe.</span>

[[The end->Credits]]


:: 4.8 Comes apart [between] {"position":"2000,850","size":"100,100"}
<span class="act">Ending · Comes apart</span>

The windows start going out, all of them, one after another. The café. The party. The back steps. Iris on the armchair, last.

You try to grab one. Your hand goes right through it.

Maeve's still sitting next to you. She looks happy. Not mean about it. Just happy, like her favorite show ended exactly the way she guessed.

"That's the whole month," she says. "There's nothing left to look at."

She stands up and holds out her hand.

"Come on."

You don't want to. You go anyway.

The page goes black. There's nothing after this.

[[The end->Credits]]


:: Content note [between] {"position":"100,100","size":"100,100"}
This story deals with grief and suicide. Nothing is ever shown, but it's there.

You can stop at any time.

If you're struggling, you don't have to carry it alone. In the US, you can call or text 988 to reach the Suicide & Crisis Lifeline, any time.

